// # src/ — The Single-Page App
//
// Logline: The JavaScript that turns index.html from a static shell
//          into a router-driven SPA with theme, install box, gen
//          bar, and the background dogfight animation.
//
// Beats:
//   1. main.js — the only file in this directory. Contains:
//      a) the route table and renderRoute() dispatcher
//      b) simpleMarkdown() for rendering the pulled/*.json content
//      c) INSTALL_HTML constant (the install box, used top + bottom)
//      d) theme palette + cycle
//      e) gen bar (Gen 1-7 toggle)
//      f) the dogfight engine: AIRCRAFT_SPECS, OODA state machine
//         (Observe / Orient / Decide / Act), weapons, damage, jet
//         silhouettes, initGlobalDogfight (the main rAF loop)
//
// Why one file (not many small ones): the dogfight is a single
// concept — an OODA state machine coupled to 7 generations of
// aircraft, 5+ weapon classes, particle systems, wreckage, and a
// rAF loop. Splitting it across files would add import plumbing
// without clarifying intent. The router, theme, and dogfight are
// three separate concerns, but they share enough globals (theme
// colors, canvas refs) that a single bundled file is the smallest
// unit that still reads as one program.
//
// Future split candidates (if the file grows further): extract
// dogfight into src/dogfight/ (state.js, render.js, weapons.js,
// gen.js, init.js) and theme into src/theme.js.
